.TH BTOON 1 "November 2026" "btoon 0.1.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
btoon \- convert between JSON and the BTOON binary format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B btoon encode
.RI [ IN.json | \- ]
.RI [ OUT.btoon | \- ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B btoon decode
.RI [ IN.btoon | \- ]
.RI [ OUT.json | \- ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B btoon info
.RI [ IN.btoon | \- ]
.br
.B btoon
.BR \-\-version " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
BTOON is MessagePack with a columnar encoding for arrays of uniform objects, extra types
(timestamps, big integers, float vectors) and optional compression/HMAC envelopes.
.B btoon
converts JSON documents to canonical BTOON and back, and describes BTOON files.
A missing or \fB\-\fR path means standard input/output.
.PP
Values JSON can't represent are written as single-key tagged objects, which are
recognized again by \fBencode\fR:
\fB{"$binary": "<base64>"}\fR, \fB{"$timestamp": "2024-01-01T00:00:00Z"}\fR (RFC 3339; the offset is kept),
\fB{"$date": <ms>}\fR, \fB{"$datetime": "<ns>"}\fR, \fB{"$bigint": "<decimal>"}\fR,
\fB{"$float": "NaN"}\fR, \fB{"$f32": [...]}\fR, \fB{"$f64": [...]}\fR, \fB{"$ext": [type, "<base64>"]}\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-compress [ =\fIALGO\fR ]
Wrap the output in a compression envelope.
.I ALGO
is zlib (the default), lz4, zstd, brotli or snappy, depending on the build. Decoding
detects envelopes automatically.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tabular
Disable the columnar encoding. The output is then plain canonical MessagePack.
.TP
.BI \-\-hmac\-key\-file " FILE"
When encoding, sign with HMAC-SHA256 using the bytes of
.IR FILE .
When decoding, require and verify a signature made with that key.
.TP
.B \-\-compact
Write single-line JSON when decoding.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tags
Don't interpret \fB$\fR-tagged objects when encoding.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a conversion error (the message includes the BTOON error code, for
example \fBtruncated\fR or \fBauthentication_failed\fR), and 2 on a usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
btoon encode data.json data.btoon \-\-compress
btoon decode data.btoon \- | jq .
btoon info data.btoon
cat data.json | btoon encode \- \- | btoon decode \- \- \-\-compact
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR btoon\-convert (1),
.BR btoon\-schema (1).
The format specification is at https://github.com/BTOON-project/btoon-core/blob/main/docs/SPEC.md
